{"schema_version": "marine_pump_page_layout_v2_1", "parser_version": "marine_pump_pdfplumber_layout_v2_1", "doc_id": "MP001", "document_split": "build_train", "source_family_id": "ABS", "publisher": "ABS", "title": "Guidance Notes on Equipment Condition Monitoring Techniques", "source_url": "https://ww2.eagle.org/content/dam/eagle/rules-and-guides/current/design_and_analysis/224-GN-EquipCndMonitoring/Equipment_Condition_Monitoring_GN_e.pdf", "source_tier": "A", "pump_type": "mixed_rotating_machinery", "service": "marine_machinery_condition_monitoring", "applicability_scope": "泵系证据仅限文中明确适用于泵或通用旋转机械且机理可迁移的陈述", "local_file": "data/source_docs/marine_pump/raw/ABS_Equipment_Condition_Monitoring_2016.pdf", "document_sha256": "47532659F8CCBE399ACC021F16DD1165935E90967B9B0A38CEDB97B0F07AC2E1", "pdf_page_number": 52, "page_width": 595.276, "page_height": 841.89, "page_text": "                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n       Section 5 Dynamic Monitoring                                       5       \n                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n                         Equipment (1)     Good     Fair   Low Alarm High Alarm   \n                                                            (4,5,7)  (4,5,8)      \n                  Vertical Pump (5' - 8' Height) < 0.250 0.250–0.400 0.400 0.600  \n                                                                                  \n                  Vertical Pump (0' - 5' Height) < 0.200 0.200–0.300 0.300 0.450  \n                  General Purpose Horizontal Pump Direct < 0.200 0.200–0.300 0.300 0.450\n                  Coupled                                                         \n                  Boiler Feed Pump         < 0.200 0.200–0.300 0.300 0.450        \n                                                                                  \n                  Hydraulic Pump           < 0.125 0.125–0.200 0.200 0.300        \n                                                                                  \n                  Notes:                                                          \n                  1    Applicable for equipment speeds 600 to 60,000 RPM          \n                  2    Measurements obtained through accelerometer or velocity pickup as close to bearing housing as\n                       practicable.                                               \n                  3    Equipment is not mounted on vibration isolators. For equipment mounted on vibration isolators,\n                       consider increasing Alarm Points 30% to 50% higher.        \n                  4    Set motor alarm the same as for equipment unless otherwise noted in Table.\n                                                                                  \n                  5    For individual external reduction gears, set Alarm Points 25% higher than for the equipment they are\n                       attached to.                                               \n                  6    These criteria are based on applied experience from the ABS PM Program and Technical Associates of\n                       Charlotte, Inc.                                            \n                  7    Equipment requires maintenance to determine cause of high vibration and to repair.\n                  8    Equipment failure is imminent and should be shut down so as to determine cause of high vibration and\n                       to repair.                                                 \n                                                                                  \n       2.4  Shock Pulse Analysis                                                  \n            Shock pulse analysis is used to monitor roller bearings, impact tools, and internal combustion engine\n            valves or components for which metal-to-metal contact is a source of wear. Measurements are taken of the\n            impact of rollers with the bearing raceway or any other rolling contact between equipment components\n            producing a shock pulse reading that changes as the conditions within the bearing or component\n            deteriorate. This technique uses a shock pulse analyzer that is set up specifically for the type and size of\n            bearings being tested and is fed a signal from an accelerometer placed on a bearing housing. It can identify\n            issues such as lubricant problems, problems with oil seals and packings, incorrect bearing installation or\n            alignment. It is based upon the principle that bearing damage can excite the bearing ring frequency which\n            vibrates at a precise frequency based upon the bearing geometry. The frequencies are somewhere between\n            8 kHz to 30 kHz. This technique is reported to work well on bearings by themselves but has some serious\n            limitation on bearings in gearboxes, pumps, motors, etc., because of the other “normal” frequencies that\n            are in most common machines, such as blade pass frequency, gear mesh frequency, and slot pass\n            frequency, for example. Shock pulse analysis should be used in conjunction with other methods (i.e.,\n            spectrum analysis, time-waveform analysis, etc.) in the assessment of bearing damage. A limit of 30.0 dB\n            has been used in the industry for the shock pulse aspects of bearing damage assessment. Placement of the\n            Shock Pulse Measurement probe is to be in the load zone of the bearing, which may not be possible and\n            could be dangerous because of coupling guards and other rotating components on the machinery.\n            ●  Typical P-F interval: Weeks to months                              \n            ●  Skill level: Trained and experienced technician                    \n            2.4.1 Advantages                                                      \n                 Advantages of this technique include the following:              \n                                                                                  \n                 i)   Test equipment is portable and easy to operate.             \n                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n                                                                                  \n       ABS GUIDANCE NOTES ON EQUIPMENT CONDITION MONITORING TECHNIQUES • 2016 52  \n                                                                                  \n                                                                                  ", "page_text_sha256": "051e3fedc5e84b46c4c9f4d2814d116427afc8ee4c16835952c164120cb53825", "source_language": "en", "source_language_confidence": 1.0, "language_detection_method": "unicode_script_ratio_v1", "printed_page": {"value": "52", "confidence": 1.0, "method": "versioned_manual_override", "bbox": null}, "visual_layout_checked": true, "text_blocks": [{"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0000", "text": "Section", "bbox": {"x0": 53.997, "top": 28.992, "x1": 86.505, "bottom": 37.992}, "reading_order": 0, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0001", "text": "5 Dynamic Monitoring", "bbox": {"x0": 107.997, "top": 28.992, "x1": 212.505, "bottom": 37.992}, "reading_order": 1, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0002", "text": "5", "bbox": {"x0": 536.272, "top": 28.992, "x1": 541.276, "bottom": 37.992}, "reading_order": 2, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0003", "text": "(1)", "bbox": {"x0": 225.055, "top": 88.099, "x1": 232.051, "bottom": 94.099}, "reading_order": 3, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0004", "text": "Equipment", "bbox": {"x0": 183.814, "top": 89.747, "x1": 222.811, "bottom": 98.747}, "reading_order": 4, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0005", "text": "Good", "bbox": {"x0": 313.255, "top": 89.747, "x1": 333.253, "bottom": 98.747}, "reading_order": 5, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0006", "text": "Fair", "bbox": {"x0": 377.545, "top": 89.747, "x1": 393.547, "bottom": 98.747}, "reading_order": 6, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0007", "text": "Low Alarm", "bbox": {"x0": 427.713, "top": 89.747, "x1": 467.97, "bottom": 98.747}, "reading_order": 7, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0008", "text": "High Alarm", "bbox": {"x0": 488.753, "top": 89.747, "x1": 531.503, "bottom": 98.747}, "reading_order": 8, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0009", "text": "(4,5,7)", "bbox": {"x0": 434.715, "top": 101.747, "x1": 458.709, "bottom": 110.747}, "reading_order": 9, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0010", "text": "(4,5,8)", "bbox": {"x0": 497.006, "top": 101.747, "x1": 521.0, "bottom": 110.747}, "reading_order": 10, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0011", "text": "Vertical Pump (5' - 8' Height)", "bbox": {"x0": 129.253, "top": 120.247, "x1": 235.228, "bottom": 129.247}, "reading_order": 11, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0012", "text": "< 0.250", "bbox": {"x0": 309.466, "top": 120.247, "x1": 337.042, "bottom": 129.247}, "reading_order": 12, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0013", "text": "0.250–0.400", "bbox": {"x0": 363.046, "top": 120.247, "x1": 408.046, "bottom": 129.247}, "reading_order": 13, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0014", "text": "0.400", "bbox": {"x0": 437.712, "top": 120.247, "x1": 457.962, "bottom": 129.247}, "reading_order": 14, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0015", "text": "0.600", "bbox": {"x0": 500.003, "top": 120.247, "x1": 520.253, "bottom": 129.247}, "reading_order": 15, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0016", "text": "Vertical Pump (0' - 5' Height)", "bbox": {"x0": 129.253, "top": 138.747, "x1": 235.228, "bottom": 147.747}, "reading_order": 16, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0017", "text": "< 0.200", "bbox": {"x0": 309.466, "top": 138.747, "x1": 337.042, "bottom": 147.747}, "reading_order": 17, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0018", "text": "0.200–0.300", "bbox": {"x0": 363.046, "top": 138.747, "x1": 408.046, "bottom": 147.747}, "reading_order": 18, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0019", "text": "0.300", "bbox": {"x0": 437.712, "top": 138.747, "x1": 457.962, "bottom": 147.747}, "reading_order": 19, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0020", "text": "0.450", "bbox": {"x0": 500.003, "top": 138.747, "x1": 520.253, "bottom": 147.747}, "reading_order": 20, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0021", "text": "General Purpose Horizontal Pump Direct", "bbox": {"x0": 129.253, "top": 157.247, "x1": 277.726, "bottom": 166.247}, "reading_order": 21, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0022", "text": "< 0.200", "bbox": {"x0": 309.466, "top": 157.247, "x1": 337.042, "bottom": 166.247}, "reading_order": 22, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0023", "text": "0.200–0.300", "bbox": {"x0": 363.046, "top": 157.247, "x1": 408.046, "bottom": 166.247}, "reading_order": 23, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0024", "text": "0.300", "bbox": {"x0": 437.712, "top": 157.247, "x1": 457.962, "bottom": 166.247}, "reading_order": 24, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0025", "text": "0.450", "bbox": {"x0": 500.003, "top": 157.247, "x1": 520.253, "bottom": 166.247}, "reading_order": 25, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0026", "text": "Coupled", "bbox": {"x0": 129.253, "top": 169.247, "x1": 159.754, "bottom": 178.247}, "reading_order": 26, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0027", "text": "Boiler Feed Pump", "bbox": {"x0": 129.253, "top": 187.747, "x1": 194.755, "bottom": 196.747}, "reading_order": 27, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0028", "text": "< 0.200", "bbox": {"x0": 309.466, "top": 187.747, "x1": 337.042, "bottom": 196.747}, "reading_order": 28, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0029", "text": "0.200–0.300", "bbox": {"x0": 363.046, "top": 187.747, "x1": 408.046, "bottom": 196.747}, "reading_order": 29, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0030", "text": "0.300", "bbox": {"x0": 437.712, "top": 187.747, "x1": 457.962, "bottom": 196.747}, "reading_order": 30, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0031", "text": "0.450", "bbox": {"x0": 500.003, "top": 187.747, "x1": 520.253, "bottom": 196.747}, "reading_order": 31, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0032", "text": "Hydraulic Pump", "bbox": {"x0": 129.253, "top": 206.247, "x1": 188.5, "bottom": 215.247}, "reading_order": 32, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0033", "text": "< 0.125", "bbox": {"x0": 309.466, "top": 206.247, "x1": 337.042, "bottom": 215.247}, "reading_order": 33, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0034", "text": "0.125–0.200", "bbox": {"x0": 363.046, "top": 206.247, "x1": 408.046, "bottom": 215.247}, "reading_order": 34, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0035", "text": "0.200", "bbox": {"x0": 437.712, "top": 206.247, "x1": 457.962, "bottom": 215.247}, "reading_order": 35, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0036", "text": "0.300", "bbox": {"x0": 500.003, "top": 206.247, "x1": 520.253, "bottom": 215.247}, "reading_order": 36, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0037", "text": "Notes:", "bbox": {"x0": 128.997, "top": 228.747, "x1": 152.496, "bottom": 237.747}, "reading_order": 37, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0038", "text": "1", "bbox": {"x0": 128.997, "top": 245.247, "x1": 133.497, "bottom": 254.247}, "reading_order": 38, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0039", "text": "Applicable for equipment speeds 600 to 60,000 RPM", "bbox": {"x0": 164.997, "top": 245.247, "x1": 356.985, "bottom": 254.247}, "reading_order": 39, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0040", "text": "2", "bbox": {"x0": 128.997, "top": 261.747, "x1": 133.497, "bottom": 270.747}, "reading_order": 40, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0041", "text": "Measurements obtained through accelerometer or velocity pickup as close to bearing housing as", "bbox": {"x0": 164.997, "top": 261.747, "x1": 541.278, "bottom": 270.747}, "reading_order": 41, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0042", "text": "practicable.", "bbox": {"x0": 165.0, "top": 272.247, "x1": 206.733, "bottom": 281.247}, "reading_order": 42, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0043", "text": "3", "bbox": {"x0": 129.0, "top": 288.747, "x1": 133.5, "bottom": 297.747}, "reading_order": 43, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0044", "text": "Equipment is not mounted on vibration isolators. For equipment mounted on vibration isolators,", "bbox": {"x0": 165.0, "top": 288.747, "x1": 541.353, "bottom": 297.747}, "reading_order": 44, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0045", "text": "consider increasing Alarm Points 30% to 50% higher.", "bbox": {"x0": 164.999, "top": 299.247, "x1": 358.481, "bottom": 308.247}, "reading_order": 45, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0046", "text": "4", "bbox": {"x0": 128.999, "top": 315.747, "x1": 133.499, "bottom": 324.747}, "reading_order": 46, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0047", "text": "Set motor alarm the same as for equipment unless otherwise noted in Table.", "bbox": {"x0": 164.999, "top": 315.747, "x1": 437.582, "bottom": 324.747}, "reading_order": 47, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0048", "text": "5", "bbox": {"x0": 128.999, "top": 332.247, "x1": 133.499, "bottom": 341.247}, "reading_order": 48, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0049", "text": "For individual external reduction gears, set Alarm Points 25% higher than for the equipment they are", "bbox": {"x0": 164.999, "top": 332.247, "x1": 541.271, "bottom": 341.247}, "reading_order": 49, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0050", "text": "attached to.", "bbox": {"x0": 165.004, "top": 342.747, "x1": 206.494, "bottom": 351.747}, "reading_order": 50, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0051", "text": "6", "bbox": {"x0": 129.004, "top": 359.247, "x1": 133.504, "bottom": 368.247}, "reading_order": 51, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0052", "text": "These criteria are based on applied experience from the ABS PM Program and Technical Associates of", "bbox": {"x0": 165.004, "top": 359.247, "x1": 541.339, "bottom": 368.247}, "reading_order": 52, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0053", "text": "Charlotte, Inc.", "bbox": {"x0": 165.002, "top": 369.747, "x1": 216.743, "bottom": 378.747}, "reading_order": 53, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0054", "text": "7", "bbox": {"x0": 129.002, "top": 386.247, "x1": 133.502, "bottom": 395.247}, "reading_order": 54, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0055", "text": "Equipment requires maintenance to determine cause of high vibration and to repair.", "bbox": {"x0": 165.002, "top": 386.247, "x1": 465.449, "bottom": 395.247}, "reading_order": 55, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0056", "text": "8", "bbox": {"x0": 129.002, "top": 402.747, "x1": 133.502, "bottom": 411.747}, "reading_order": 56, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0057", "text": "Equipment failure is imminent and should be shut down so as to determine cause of high vibration and", "bbox": {"x0": 165.002, "top": 402.747, "x1": 541.301, "bottom": 411.747}, "reading_order": 57, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0058", "text": "to repair.", "bbox": {"x0": 165.004, "top": 413.247, "x1": 196.99, "bottom": 422.247}, "reading_order": 58, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0059", "text": "2.4", "bbox": {"x0": 53.996, "top": 438.99, "x1": 69.286, "bottom": 449.99}, "reading_order": 59, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0060", "text": "Shock Pulse Analysis", "bbox": {"x0": 89.999, "top": 438.99, "x1": 203.717, "bottom": 449.99}, "reading_order": 60, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0061", "text": "Shock pulse analysis is used to monitor roller bearings, impact tools, and internal combustion engine", "bbox": {"x0": 90.002, "top": 454.747, "x1": 541.261, "bottom": 465.247}, "reading_order": 61, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0062", "text": "valves or components for which metal-to-metal contact is a source of wear. Measurements are taken of the", "bbox": {"x0": 89.997, "top": 466.747, "x1": 541.381, "bottom": 477.247}, "reading_order": 62, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0063", "text": "impact of rollers with the bearing raceway or any other rolling contact between equipment components", "bbox": {"x0": 89.999, "top": 478.747, "x1": 541.268, "bottom": 489.247}, "reading_order": 63, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0064", "text": "producing a shock pulse reading that changes as the conditions within the bearing or component", "bbox": {"x0": 89.995, "top": 490.747, "x1": 541.38, "bottom": 501.247}, "reading_order": 64, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0065", "text": "deteriorate. This technique uses a shock pulse analyzer that is set up specifically for the type and size of", "bbox": {"x0": 89.996, "top": 502.747, "x1": 541.255, "bottom": 513.247}, "reading_order": 65, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0066", "text": "bearings being tested and is fed a signal from an accelerometer placed on a bearing housing. It can identify", "bbox": {"x0": 90.001, "top": 514.747, "x1": 541.417, "bottom": 525.247}, "reading_order": 66, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0067", "text": "issues such as lubricant problems, problems with oil seals and packings, incorrect bearing installation or", "bbox": {"x0": 89.998, "top": 526.747, "x1": 541.267, "bottom": 537.247}, "reading_order": 67, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0068", "text": "alignment. It is based upon the principle that bearing damage can excite the bearing ring frequency which", "bbox": {"x0": 90.002, "top": 538.747, "x1": 541.429, "bottom": 549.247}, "reading_order": 68, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0069", "text": "vibrates at a precise frequency based upon the bearing geometry. The frequencies are somewhere between", "bbox": {"x0": 90.005, "top": 550.747, "x1": 541.306, "bottom": 561.247}, "reading_order": 69, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0070", "text": "8 kHz to 30 kHz. This technique is reported to work well on bearings by themselves but has some serious", "bbox": {"x0": 90.004, "top": 562.747, "x1": 541.263, "bottom": 573.247}, "reading_order": 70, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0071", "text": "limitation on bearings in gearboxes, pumps, motors, etc., because of the other “normal” frequencies that", "bbox": {"x0": 90.002, "top": 574.747, "x1": 541.397, "bottom": 585.247}, "reading_order": 71, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0072", "text": "are in most common machines, such as blade pass frequency, gear mesh frequency, and slot pass", "bbox": {"x0": 89.995, "top": 586.747, "x1": 541.285, "bottom": 597.247}, "reading_order": 72, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0073", "text": "frequency, for example. Shock pulse analysis should be used in conjunction with other methods (i.e.,", "bbox": {"x0": 89.996, "top": 598.747, "x1": 541.275, "bottom": 609.247}, "reading_order": 73, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0074", "text": "spectrum analysis, time-waveform analysis, etc.) in the assessment of bearing damage. A limit of 30.0 dB", "bbox": {"x0": 90.001, "top": 610.747, "x1": 541.26, "bottom": 621.247}, "reading_order": 74, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0075", "text": "has been used in the industry for the shock pulse aspects of bearing damage assessment. Placement of the", "bbox": {"x0": 89.996, "top": 622.747, "x1": 541.234, "bottom": 633.247}, "reading_order": 75, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0076", "text": "Shock Pulse Measurement probe is to be in the load zone of the bearing, which may not be possible and", "bbox": {"x0": 90.005, "top": 634.747, "x1": 541.243, "bottom": 645.247}, "reading_order": 76, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0077", "text": "could be dangerous because of coupling guards and other rotating components on the machinery.", "bbox": {"x0": 90.002, "top": 646.747, "x1": 496.993, "bottom": 657.247}, "reading_order": 77, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0078", "text": "● Typical P-F interval: Weeks to months", "bbox": {"x0": 90.002, "top": 669.24, "x1": 271.138, "bottom": 679.747}, "reading_order": 78, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0079", "text": "● Skill level: Trained and experienced technician", "bbox": {"x0": 90.002, "top": 687.24, "x1": 304.423, "bottom": 697.747}, "reading_order": 79, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0080", "text": "2.4.1 Advantages", "bbox": {"x0": 90.003, "top": 705.491, "x1": 181.593, "bottom": 715.491}, "reading_order": 80, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0081", "text": "Advantages of this technique include the following:", "bbox": {"x0": 125.995, "top": 720.247, "x1": 343.555, "bottom": 730.747}, "reading_order": 81, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0082", "text": "i)", "bbox": {"x0": 125.995, "top": 742.747, "x1": 132.411, "bottom": 753.247}, "reading_order": 82, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0083", "text": "Test equipment is portable and easy to operate.", "bbox": {"x0": 162.0, "top": 742.747, "x1": 358.98, "bottom": 753.247}, "reading_order": 83, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0084", "text": "GUIDANCE NOTES ON EQUIPMENT CONDITION MONITORING TECHNIQUES • 2016", "bbox": {"x0": 77.004, "top": 787.056, "x1": 433.539, "bottom": 796.056}, "reading_order": 84, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0085", "text": "52", "bbox": {"x0": 531.266, "top": 787.056, "x1": 541.274, "bottom": 796.056}, "reading_order": 85, "block_type": "text_line"}, {"block_id": "MP001:p0052:b0086", "text": "ABS", "bbox": {"x0": 54.0, "top": 787.938, "x1": 74.502, "bottom": 796.938}, "reading_order": 86, "block_type": "text_line"}], "tables": [{"table_id": "MP001:p0052:t00", "bbox": {"x0": 126.0, "top": 85.0, "x1": 541.276, "bottom": 220.0}, "column_names": ["Equipment (1)", "Good", "Fair", "Low Alarm (4,5,7)", "High Alarm (4,5,8)"], "column_roles": ["unclassified", "unclassified", "unclassified", "unclassified", "unclassified"], "rows": [{"row_id": "MP001:p0052:t00:r000", "row_group_id": "MP001:p0052:t00:r000", "row_index": 0, "cells": [{"cell_id": "MP001:p0052:t00:r000:c00", "table_id": "MP001:p0052:t00", "row_id": "MP001:p0052:t00:r000", "row_group_id": "MP001:p0052:t00:r000", "row_index": 0, "column_index": 0, "column_name": "Equipment (1)", "column_role": "unclassified", "text": "Equipment (1)", "page_text_start": 606, "page_text_e